<!--DOM stands for Document Object Model. When the browser loads an HTML page, it
creates a tree-like representation of all the elements: the <body>, the <p> tags, the <button> tags, everything. This tree is the DOM.

      <!doctype html>
      <html>
        <body>
          <p id="text">Click the button to make me blue!</p>
          <button
            onclick="document.getElementById('text').style.color = 'blue'"
          >
            Turn blue
          </button>
        </body>
      </html>

JavaScript can read and modify this tree. That's how it changes text, adds elements, removes them or updates styles.